// Copy to WhoopSecrets.xcconfig (gitignored) and fill in your own WHOOP developer app's values.
// Register at developer.whoop.com; set the redirect URL to noop://whoop-oauth and request the
// scopes read:recovery read:cycles read:sleep read:workout read:profile offline.
//
// THE CLIENT SECRET ENDS UP IN THE BUILT APP, and that is a real weakness rather than a detail.
// WHOOP's token endpoint requires client_secret and their flow has no PKCE-only public-client mode,
// so a mobile app has no way to hold this safely: anyone who unpacks the .ipa has it. Keeping the
// file out of the repository is the whole of what this app can do about it. For a build you install
// on your own phone that is an acceptable trade; for a distributed build it is not, and the honest
// fix is a token exchange on a server you control.
WHOOP_CLIENT_ID = your_client_id_here
WHOOP_CLIENT_SECRET = your_client_secret_here
// See the note in BundleId.xcconfig: the $() keeps the "//" from starting a comment.
WHOOP_REDIRECT_URI = noop:/$()/whoop-oauth
